f0: $ G ⇒ (∃ x1 ∃ x2 ∃ x3 ∃ x4 ∃ x5 ∃ x6 ∃ x7 ∃ x8 ∃ x9 ∃ x0 ∃ e ∃ h (t1 = x1 ∧ t2 = x2 ∧ t3 = x3 ∧ t4 = x4 ∧ t5 = x5 ∧ c = x6 ∧ d = x7 ∧ z = ⟨ kc_pi , scons x9 (scons x0 ∅) ⟩ ∧ ra_add x7 x3 x8 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_closed x8 x9 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_sinst x1 ⟨ kc_nz , ∅ ⟩ x2 x8 x9 e ∈ lrel ∧ ra_deq x6 e e ⟨ kc_srt , scons h ∅ ⟩ ∈ J ∧ ra_ulevel x4 h ∈ lrel2 ∧ ra_cwf x1 x2 x3 x4 x5 ⟨ kc_cons , scons e (scons x6 ∅) ⟩ ⟨ kc_s , scons x7 ∅ ⟩ x0 ∈ lrel3 J)) → etel u (dnf u M) z w a ⊆ etel u (dnf u M) z w b $ by imp_intro [e0b]

--| `lrel_cwf_mono`, the case `cwf_pi_rec`: through `b7_cm_c1`.
lemma b7_cm_c1r {i x1 x2 x3 x4 x5 x6 x7 x8 x9 x0 e v h: set} (G: hyps) (J M X0: class) (u w a b t1 t2 t3 t4 t5 c d z k j: set): $ G ⇒ crn j ⊆ b7_cm u M w J t1 t2 t3 t4 t5 X0 $ > $ G ⇒ z = ⟨ k , j ⟩ $ > $ G ⇒ z ∊ trees ω $ > $ G ⇒ d ∊ trees ω $ > $ G ⇒ w ∊ lvals $ > $ G ⇒ a ∊ fseq u $ > $ G ⇒ b ∊ fseq u $ > $ G ⇒ ∀ i (i ∊ nadd (fv nvf d) (fv nvf t3) → fv a i = fv b i) $ > $ G ⇒ b7_hw t1 X0 a b d t3 $ > $ G ⇒ uadm u $ > $ G ⇒ (∃ x1 ∃ x2 ∃ x3 ∃ x4 ∃ x5 ∃ x6 ∃ x7 ∃ x8 ∃ x9 ∃ x0 ∃ e ∃ v ∃ h (t1 = x1 ∧ t2 = x2 ∧ t3 = x3 ∧ t4 = x4 ∧ t5 = x5 ∧ c = x6 ∧ d = x7 ∧ z = ⟨ kc_pi , scons x9 (scons x0 ∅) ⟩ ∧ ra_add x7 x3 x8 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_sinst x1 ⟨ kc_nz , ∅ ⟩ x2 x8 x9 e ∈ lrel ∧ ra_deq x6 e e ⟨ kc_srt , scons h ∅ ⟩ ∈ J ∧ ra_ulevel x4 h ∈ lrel2 ∧ ra_ipos x1 x2 x3 x7 x9 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_inst ⟨ kc_nz , ∅ ⟩ x0 ⟨ kc_srt , scons ⟨ kc_lz , ∅ ⟩ ∅ ⟩ v ∈ lrel ∧ ra_lift ⟨ kc_s , scons ⟨ kc_nz , ∅ ⟩ ∅ ⟩ ⟨ kc_nz , ∅ ⟩ v x0 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_cwf x1 x2 x3 x4 x5 ⟨ kc_cons , scons e (scons x6 ∅) ⟩ ⟨ kc_s , scons x7 ∅ ⟩ x0 ∈ lrel3 J)) → etel u (dnf u M) z w a ⊆ etel u (dnf u M) z w b $
----
